**P2 · Avoid splitting UTF-8 at the detector boundary (2/2)**

A valid multi-byte UTF-8 character can straddle the 64-KiB sample boundary. With 65,535 ASCII bytes before a 3-byte character, the exact upstream tree produces corrupted preview text. Detect larger files from the complete stream, bounded by the existing preview-size check, while sampling smaller files in full.

```suggestion
            Encoding.RegisterProvider(CodePagesEncodingProvider.Instance);
            DetectionResult result;
            if (fs.Length > CharsetSampleSizeBytes)
            {
                result = await CharsetDetector.DetectFromStreamAsync(fs, maxReadableFileSizeBytes, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
            }
            else
            {
                int sampleSize = (int)fs.Length;
                var sample = new byte[sampleSize];
                int sampleRead = await fs.ReadAtLeastAsync(sample, sampleSize, throwOnEndOfStream: false, cancellationToken).ConfigureAwait(false);
                result = CharsetDetector.DetectFromBytes(sampleRead == sample.Length ? sample : sample[..sampleRead]);
            }

            Encoding encodingToUse = result.Detected?.Encoding ?? Encoding.UTF8;
```
